{"id": "mimiciv-001", "level": "noob", "nl_description": "We need a databse for a hospitel. The hospital has pashents who come in and get admited. Each pashent has a gender and approximate age. Admitions have a start time (when they came in) and end time (when they left) and a type like emergency or elective. If someone died in the hospitel we record that too. Some pashents go to the ICU (intensive care unit) after being admited. Each ICU stay has a start time, end time, and a length of stay in days. Most pashent ICU stays are pretty short -- most are under 4 days but some stay much longer. We also want to track what diagnoses pashents recieved using standard medical codes.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "PATIENT", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "gender", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "dod", "data_type": "DATE"}]}, {"name": "ADMISSION", "pk": "hadm_id", "columns": [{"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "admittime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "deathtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admission_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "ICU_STAY", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "first_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "intime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "outtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "los", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "DIAGNOSIS", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "seq_num", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "icd_code", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "icd_version", "data_type": "INT"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "ADMISSION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "DIAGNOSIS", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"PATIENT.anchor_age": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 63.0, "std": 17.0}}, "ICU_STAY.los": {"family": "exponential", "params": {"rate": 0.33}}}}
{"id": "mimiciv-002", "level": "noob", "nl_description": "A hospital patient record system. Patients have a unique id, biological sex, and there age at a certain reference point. When a patient is admited to the hospital, the admision records when they came in and when they left, and if they were dischared to home, another facility, etc. The hospitel keeps track of medicasion presciptions for each admission -- the drug name, when they started and stoped taking it, how many doses per day, and what route it was adminstered (oral, IV, etc). They also want to track lab tests like blood tests with the test result value and a flag for if its abnormal. All lab tests and prescriptions are linked back to the admision they happend during.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "PATIENT", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "gender", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "ADMISSION", "pk": "hadm_id", "columns": [{"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "admittime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admission_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "discharge_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "PRESCRIPTION", "pk": "pharmacy_id", "columns": [{"name": "pharmacy_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "starttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "stoptime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "drug", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "drug_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_val_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_unit_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "route", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "doses_per_24_hrs", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "LAB_EVENT", "pk": "labevent_id", "columns": [{"name": "labevent_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ref_range_lower", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "ref_range_upper", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "flag", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "ADMISSION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "PRESCRIPTION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "PRESCRIPTION", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"PATIENT.anchor_age": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 63.0, "std": 17.0}}}}
{"id": "mimiciv-003", "level": "intermediate", "nl_description": "ICU patient monitoring database from a single academic medical center. Patients have a de-identified reference year and age at that reference point -- the age is clipped at 91 for privacy. Hospital admissions record admission type (emergency, elective, urgent are the main ones), insurance payer, language, marital status, race, and whether the patient died in hospital. ICU stays are nested within admissions: each has a care unit type at admission and discharge, and a length of stay in fractional days. ICU length of stay is heavily right-skewed -- about three-quarters of patients leave within four days. An item dictionary defines the clinical measurement parameters: each item has a label, category, linked table, and normal value range. Chart events record vital sign measurements taken during ICU stays; each row has a timestamp, the measurement item, a text value, numeric value where applicable, and a warning flag. All vital signs have numeric values.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "PATIENT", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "gender", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year_group", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dod", "data_type": "DATE"}]}, {"name": "ADMISSION", "pk": "hadm_id", "columns": [{"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "admittime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "deathtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admission_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "discharge_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "marital_status", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "race", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "ICU_STAY", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "first_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "last_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "intime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "outtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "los", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "D_ITEM", "pk": "itemid", "columns": [{"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "label", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "abbreviation", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "linksto", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "unitname", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "param_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "lownormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "highnormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "CHART_EVENT", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "storetime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "warning", "data_type": "INT"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "ADMISSION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "CHART_EVENT", "referencing_column": "stay_id", "referred_table": "ICU_STAY"}, {"referencing_table": "CHART_EVENT", "referencing_column": "itemid", "referred_table": "D_ITEM"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"PATIENT.anchor_age": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 63.0, "std": 17.0}}, "ICU_STAY.los": {"family": "exponential", "params": {"rate": 0.33}}}}
{"id": "mimiciv-004", "level": "intermediate", "nl_description": "Clinical data schema for a tertiary care hospital. Patients undergo hospital admissions; a hospital stay may contain one or more ICU episodes. Lab results are generated throughout a hospital stay: each lab event records the test identifier, the specimen draw time, entry time, numeric result, the reported value string, units, reference range, abnormality flag, and a STAT vs routine priority. Prescriptions are another major component: medication records include the drug name and type (main medication, base, or additive), a formulary code, NDC number, product strength, form, dosage value and units, dispensed quantity, and route. Diagnoses are recorded as ICD code assignments per admission with a sequence number (sequence 1 = principal diagnosis). There is an item dictionary for both ICU chart items and laboratory test items -- dictionary entries carry a label, category, unit, and normal range.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "PATIENT", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "gender", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "dod", "data_type": "DATE"}]}, {"name": "ADMISSION", "pk": "hadm_id", "columns": [{"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "admittime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admission_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "marital_status", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "ICU_STAY", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "first_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "last_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "intime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "outtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "los", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "D_ITEM", "pk": "itemid", "columns": [{"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "label", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "unitname", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "lownormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "highnormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "LAB_EVENT", "pk": "labevent_id", "columns": [{"name": "labevent_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "storetime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ref_range_lower", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "ref_range_upper", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "flag", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "priority", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "PRESCRIPTION", "pk": "pharmacy_id", "columns": [{"name": "pharmacy_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "starttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "stoptime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "drug_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "drug", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "formulary_drug_cd", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ndc", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "prod_strength", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_val_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_unit_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_val_disp", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_unit_disp", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "doses_per_24_hrs", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "route", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "DIAGNOSIS", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "seq_num", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "icd_code", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "icd_version", "data_type": "INT"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "ADMISSION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "itemid", "referred_table": "D_ITEM"}, {"referencing_table": "PRESCRIPTION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "PRESCRIPTION", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "DIAGNOSIS", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"PATIENT.anchor_age": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 63.0, "std": 17.0}}, "ICU_STAY.los": {"family": "exponential", "params": {"rate": 0.33}}}}
{"id": "mimiciv-005", "level": "expert", "nl_description": "Relational schema for a large-scale single-center clinical database covering hospital and ICU care at a quaternary academic medical center. Patient registry: ~300K patients with de-identified demographics. Ages are anchor-based: anchor_age is the patient's age at anchor_year, both shifted to preserve privacy; patients aged 91 and older are grouped. Two modules: hospital-level (hosp) and ICU-level (icu). Hospital module tables: admissions (~430K rows), lab events (~118M rows), prescriptions (~18.5M rows), diagnoses (~4.7M rows). ICU module tables: ICU stays (~73K rows), chart events (~320M rows), an item dictionary (3,835 items). Admission type distribution: emergency ~50%, elective ~30%, urgent ~10%, other ~10%. In-hospital mortality ~8-10%. ICU length of stay in fractional days is exponentially distributed (right-skewed, mean approximately 3 days). Patient age at admission is approximately normal with mean 63 and std 17, clipped at [18, 91]. Lab events have separate reference range bounds and an abnormality flag. Chart events link to ICU stays via stay_id and to the item dictionary via itemid. The item dictionary specifies the parameter type (Numeric, Text, Date/Time) and the clinical linkage table. Diagnoses are ICD-coded (version 9 for pre-2015, version 10 after), ordered by clinical sequence within each admission.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "PATIENT", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "gender", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year_group", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dod", "data_type": "DATE"}]}, {"name": "ADMISSION", "pk": "hadm_id", "columns": [{"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "admittime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "deathtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admission_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admit_provider_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "discharge_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "marital_status", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "race", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "edregtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "edouttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "ICU_STAY", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "first_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "last_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "intime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "outtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "los", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "D_ITEM", "pk": "itemid", "columns": [{"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "label", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "abbreviation", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "linksto", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "unitname", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "param_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "lownormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "highnormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "CHART_EVENT", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "storetime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "warning", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "LAB_EVENT", "pk": "labevent_id", "columns": [{"name": "labevent_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "storetime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ref_range_lower", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "ref_range_upper", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "flag", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "priority", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "comments", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "PRESCRIPTION", "pk": "pharmacy_id", "columns": [{"name": "pharmacy_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "poe_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "poe_seq", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "starttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "stoptime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "drug_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "drug", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "formulary_drug_cd", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "gsn", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ndc", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "prod_strength", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_val_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_unit_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_val_disp", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_unit_disp", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "doses_per_24_hrs", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "route", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "DIAGNOSIS", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "seq_num", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "icd_code", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "icd_version", "data_type": "INT"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "ADMISSION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "ICU_STAY", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "CHART_EVENT", "referencing_column": "stay_id", "referred_table": "ICU_STAY"}, {"referencing_table": "CHART_EVENT", "referencing_column": "itemid", "referred_table": "D_ITEM"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "LAB_EVENT", "referencing_column": "itemid", "referred_table": "D_ITEM"}, {"referencing_table": "PRESCRIPTION", "referencing_column": "subject_id", "referred_table": "PATIENT"}, {"referencing_table": "PRESCRIPTION", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}, {"referencing_table": "DIAGNOSIS", "referencing_column": "hadm_id", "referred_table": "ADMISSION"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"PATIENT.anchor_age": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 63.0, "std": 17.0}}, "ICU_STAY.los": {"family": "exponential", "params": {"rate": 0.33}}}}
{"id": "mimiciv-006", "level": "expert", "nl_description": "Schema for a de-identified critical care database from a single US academic medical center. Two organizational modules: the hospital module covers all admitted patients, admissions, laboratory orders, prescriptions, and coded diagnoses; the ICU module covers intensive care unit stays, high-frequency bedside monitoring data, and an item dictionary. Core structural properties: every ICU stay has a parent admission; every admission has a parent patient. The patient record uses a reference-year anchor system for de-identification: anchor_age is patient age at anchor_year, which is itself shifted; patients in the 91+ age group have their exact age suppressed. Admission records nine administrative attributes besides timestamps: type, location, payer, language, marital status, race, ED registration and exit times, and an in-hospital mortality binary flag. The item dictionary is shared between chart events and lab events via itemid FK. Dictionary entries specify the clinical quantity (label, abbreviation), its storage location (linksto field), category, unit, and two normal range bounds. Chart events (~320M rows) store per-second bedside measurements; each row has charted timestamp, storage timestamp, item FK, text value, optional numeric value, and a clinician warning flag. Lab events (~118M rows) have a specimen-level linkage (specimen_id), charted and stored timestamps, numeric result, units, dual reference bounds, abnormality flag, and STAT/routine priority. Prescriptions record the full dispensing detail: POE ID and sequence, formulary code, NDC, product strength, dosing form, dispensed quantities, and administration route.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "PATIENT", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "gender", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "anchor_year_group", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dod", "data_type": "DATE"}]}, {"name": "ADMISSION", "pk": "hadm_id", "columns": [{"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "admittime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "deathtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admission_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admit_provider_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "discharge_location", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "marital_status", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "race", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "edregtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "edouttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "ICU_STAY", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "first_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "last_careunit", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "intime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "outtime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "los", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "D_ITEM", "pk": "itemid", "columns": [{"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "label", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "abbreviation", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "linksto", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "unitname", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "param_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "lownormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "highnormalvalue", "data_type": "FLOAT"}]}, {"name": "CHART_EVENT", "pk": "stay_id", "columns": [{"name": "stay_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "storetime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "warning", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "LAB_EVENT", "pk": "labevent_id", "columns": [{"name": "labevent_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "specimen_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "itemid", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "charttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "storetime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "value", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "valuenum", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "valueuom", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ref_range_lower", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "ref_range_upper", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "flag", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "priority", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "comments", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "PRESCRIPTION", "pk": "pharmacy_id", "columns": [{"name": "pharmacy_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "poe_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "poe_seq", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "starttime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "stoptime", "data_type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "drug_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "drug", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "formulary_drug_cd", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "gsn", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ndc", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "prod_strength", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_val_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dose_unit_rx", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_val_disp", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "form_unit_disp", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "doses_per_24_hrs", "data_type": "FLOAT"}, {"name": "route", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "DIAGNOSIS", "pk": "subject_id", "columns": [{"name": "subj